    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "IN APPRECIATION OF\nPILOT JOE HAMMER\nC. A.M. 30\nJUNE 29ГH - JULY 5TH\nINTERSTATE AIRLINES, INC.\nCHICAGO - - ATLANTA\nos. Hammer\nжим.\nBUL: 1\n5\nEN\nNx10%\nCENT\nAIR MAIL\n210) W. \u003e8 th\nbleveland Chist",
      "****** **\n1999,023.003\nY*********",
      "JOE HAMMER, night mail pilot on the\nInterstate Airlines Chicago, Evansville,\nSt. Louis routes, has been flying for\nInterstate for more than a year. Be-\nfore night routes were inaugurated\nApril I, 1930, Joe flew the daylight\nruns on the same route he now flys at\nnight. He is a veteran pilot with\nseveral thousand hours flying to his\ncredit. His career has been an unusu-\nally interesting one. Before he learned\nto fly he was building motorless planes\nduring his high school days. His present\nhome is in Chicago, Ill., from where he\nflys the Interstate route south, alternating with pilots John Pricer and M.\nD. Ator."
    ],
